@lang en
IMPORT `msig-cgl-record`

-- CONDITIONS 1-10 (src:178-311), in the order printed.
--
-- Duties are regulative rules (PARTY ... MUST/SHANT ...). The policy states no period in
-- days for any duty of the insured: "as soon as practicable" (3(a)), "immediately" (3(b))
-- and "promptly" (Sistership) are standards, not periods, so those rules carry no WITHIN
-- (writing-l4-rules phrasebook 5.9: a period the text does not state is not invented).
-- Whether a standard was met is a finding (NOTES.md, fork F12). The time unit of a
-- #TRACE over these rules is the day.
--
-- The periods the conditions DO state are dates computed here: three years for the audit
-- (Condition 2) and ten days for the Company's notice of cancellation (Condition 9).

§ `CONDITIONS`
-- src:178 | CONDITIONS

§§ `1. Premium`

-- The Company's "rules, rates, rating plans, premiums and minimum premiums" are not in the
-- document. The premium, the advance premium and the earned premium are therefore
-- inputs, never computed here.
-- src:180 | 1. Premium
-- src:182 | All premiums for this Policy shall be computed in accordance with the Company's rules, rates, rating plans, premiums
-- src:183 | and minimum premiums applicable to the insurance afforded herein.
@ref src:182-183
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Condition 1 — the premium computed under the Company's rules, which are not in the document` MEANS
    REFUSE "Condition 1: the premium is computed under the Company's rules, rates and rating plans, which are not in the document"

-- The advance premium is a deposit credited against the earned premium; the earned
-- premium falls due on notice; an earned premium below what was paid is returned.
-- src:185 | Premium designated in this Policy as "advance premium" is a deposit premium only which shall be credited to the
-- src:186 | amount of the earned premium due at the end of the policy period. At the close of each period (or part thereof
-- src:187 | terminating with the end of the policy period) designated in the declarations as the audit period the earned premium
-- src:188 | shall be computed for such period and, upon notice thereof to the named insured, shall become due and payable. If
-- src:189 | the total earned premium for the policy period is less than the premium previously paid, the Company shall return to
-- src:190 | the named insured the unearned portion paid by the named insured.
@ref src:185-190
GIVEN `the earned premium for the policy period` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium previously paid`            IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A premium adjustment`
`Condition 1 — the adjustment of an earned premium of` `the earned premium for the policy period` `against premium paid of` `the premium previously paid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the earned premium for the policy period` LESS THAN `the premium previously paid`
        THEN `the Company returns the unearned portion` (`the premium previously paid` MINUS `the earned premium for the policy period`)
        IF   `the earned premium for the policy period` GREATER THAN `the premium previously paid`
        THEN `the named insured pays the earned premium due` (`the earned premium for the policy period` MINUS `the premium previously paid`)
        OTHERWISE `no adjustment`

-- "at the end of the policy period and at such times during the policy period as the
-- Company may direct": no period in days.
-- src:192 | The named insured shall maintain records of such information as is necessary for premium computation, and shall
-- src:193 | send copies of such records to the Company at the end of the policy period and at such times during the policy period
-- src:194 | as the Company may direct.
@ref src:192-194
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to the policy` `An act under the policy`
`Condition 1 — the named insured sends its premium records` MEANS
    PARTY `the named insured`
    MUST  `send copies of the premium records to the Company`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§§ `2. Inspection and Audit`

-- The right to inspect is a permission with no duty and no warranty of safety: nothing a
-- claim turns on. Carried as named text.
-- src:196 | 2. Inspection and Audit
-- src:198 | The Company shall be permitted but not obligated to inspect the named insured's property and operations at any time.
-- src:199 | Neither the Company's right to make inspections nor the making thereof nor any report thereon shall constitute an
-- src:200 | undertaking, on behalf of or for the benefit of the named insured or others, to determine or warrant that such property
-- src:201 | or operations are safe or healthful, or are in compliance with any law, rule or regulation.
@ref src:198-201
`Condition 2 — inspection` MEANS
    "The Company shall be permitted but not obligated to inspect the named insured's property and operations at any time. Neither the Company's right to make inspections nor the making thereof nor any report thereon shall constitute an undertaking, on behalf of or for the benefit of the named insured or others, to determine or warrant that such property or operations are safe or healthful, or are in compliance with any law, rule or regulation."

-- "within three (3) years after the final termination": calendar years, counted to the
-- same day three years on, that day included (NOTES.md, fork F13). `add years` clamps
-- 29 February to 28 February.
-- src:203 | The Company may examine and audit the named insured's books and records at any time during the policy period and
-- src:204 | extensions thereof and within three (3) years after the final termination of this Policy, as far as they relate to the
-- src:205 | subject matter of this insurance.
@ref src:203-205
GIVEN `the final termination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Condition 2 — the last day the Company may examine and audit, after a final termination on` `the final termination` MEANS
    `add years` `the final termination` 3

@ref src:203-205
GIVEN d                       IS A DATE
      `the period begins`     IS A DATE
      `the final termination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Condition 2 — the Company may examine and audit on` d `, for a policy beginning` `the period begins` `and finally terminating` `the final termination` MEANS
        d AT LEAST `the period begins`
    AND d AT MOST  `Condition 2 — the last day the Company may examine and audit, after a final termination on` `the final termination`

§§ `3. Insured's Duties in the Event of Occurrence, Claim or Suit`

-- src:207 | 3. Insured's Duties in the Event of Occurrence, Claim or Suit
-- src:209 | (a) in the event of an occurrence, written notice containing particulars sufficient to identify the insured and also
-- src:210 | reasonably obtainable information with respect to the time, place and circumstances thereof, and the names and
-- src:211 | addresses of the injured and of available witnesses, shall be given by or for the insured to the Company or any of
-- src:212 | its authorized agents as soon as practicable.
@ref src:209-212
GIVEN notice IS A `A written notice of an occurrence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Condition 3(a) — the notice has the content and route required` notice MEANS
        notice's `in writing`
    AND notice's `contains particulars sufficient to identify the insured`
    AND notice's `contains reasonably obtainable information on the time, place and circumstances`
    AND notice's `contains the names and addresses of the injured`
    AND notice's `contains the names and addresses of available witnesses`
    AND notice's `given by or for the insured to the Company or one of its authorized agents`

-- "as soon as practicable": a standard, not a period. No WITHIN.
@ref src:209-212
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to the policy` `An act under the policy`
`Condition 3(a) — notice of an occurrence` MEANS
    PARTY `the insured`
    MUST  `give written notice of the occurrence to the Company or an authorized agent`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- "immediately": a standard, not a period. No WITHIN.
-- src:214 | (b) If claim is made or suit is brought against the insured, the insured shall immediately forward to the Company
-- src:215 | every demand, notice, summons or other process received by him or his representative.
@ref src:214-215
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to the policy` `An act under the policy`
`Condition 3(b) — forwarding of claims and process` MEANS
    PARTY `the insured`
    MUST  `forward every demand, notice, summons or other process received`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- The duty to cooperate and assist is owed "upon the Company's request" and has no act a
-- trace can stamp; it is read through Condition 4's "full compliance" finding. The
-- prohibition on voluntary payments is a SHANT; its consequence is that the payment is
-- "at his own cost", which the answer module gives effect to by leaving such sums out of
-- the ultimate net loss.
-- src:217 | (c) The insured shall cooperate with the Company and, upon the Company's request, assist in making settlements, in
-- src:218 | the conduct of suits and enforcing any right of contribution or indemnity against any person or organization who
-- src:219 | may be liable to the insured because of bodily injury or property damage with respect to which insurance is afforded
-- src:220 | under this Policy, and the insured shall attend hearings and trials and assist in securing and giving evidence and
-- src:226 | obtaining the attendance of witnesses. The insured shall not, except at his own cost, voluntarily make any payment,
-- src:227 | assume any obligation or incur any expense other than for first aid to others at the time of accident.
@ref src:226-227
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to the policy` `An act under the policy`
`Condition 3(c) — no voluntary payment, obligation or expense` MEANS
    PARTY `the insured`
    SHANT `voluntarily make a payment, assume an obligation or incur an expense other than for first aid`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the insured` BECAUSE "Condition 3(c): a voluntary payment, obligation or expense, other than first aid, is at the insured's own cost"

§§ `4. Action Against Company`

-- Two conditions precedent: full compliance with every term, and the amount finally fixed
-- by judgement after actual trial or by written agreement of all three. Read with the
-- duties above, any departure from a duty (late notice included) bars the action in full
-- (NOTES.md, finding X8 and fork F14).
-- src:229 | 4. Action Against Company
-- src:231 | No action shall lie against the Company unless, as a condition precedent thereto, there shall have been full compliance
-- src:232 | with all of the terms of this Policy, nor until the amount of the insured's obligation to pay shall have been finally
-- src:233 | determined either by judgement against the insured after actual trial or by written agreement of the insured, the claimant
-- src:234 | and the Company.
@ref src:231-234
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Condition 4 — an action lies against the Company` claim MEANS
        `for` claim `,` `there has been full compliance with all of the terms of the Policy`
    AND (   `for` claim `,` `the insured's obligation to pay has been finally determined by judgement against the insured after actual trial`
         OR `for` claim `,` `the insured's obligation to pay has been finally determined by written agreement of the insured, the claimant and the Company`)

-- A claimant holding such a judgement or agreement may recover "to the extent of the
-- insurance afforded": the same two conditions, read for the claimant. No joinder, no
-- impleading, and the insured's insolvency does not release the Company: none of these
-- changes an answer this encoding computes.
-- src:236 | Any person or organization or the legal representative thereof who has secured such judgement or written agreement
-- src:237 | shall thereafter be entitled to recover under this Policy to the extent of the insurance afforded by this Policy. No person
-- src:238 | or organization shall have any right under this Policy to join the Company as a party to any action against the insured
-- src:239 | to determine the insured's liability, nor shall the Company be impleaded by the insured or his legal representative.
-- src:240 | Bankruptcy or insolvency of the insured or of the insured's estate shall not relieve the Company of any of its obligations
-- src:241 | hereunder.
@ref src:236-237
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Condition 4 — the claimant is entitled to recover under the Policy` claim MEANS
    `Condition 4 — an action lies against the Company` claim

§§ `5. Other Insurance`

-- src:243 | 5. Other Insurance
-- src:245 | The insurance afforded by this Policy is primary insurance, except when stated to, apply in excess of or contingent
-- src:246 | upon the absence of other insurance. When this insurance is primary and the insured has other insurance which is
-- src:247 | stated to be applicable to the loss on an excess or contingent basis, the amount of the Company's liability under this
-- src:248 | Policy shall not be reduced by the existence of such other insurance.
-- src:250 | When both this insurance and other insurance apply to the loss on the same basis, whether primary, excess or
-- src:251 | contingent, the Company shall not be liable under this Policy for a greater proportion of the loss than that stated in the
-- src:252 | applicable contribution provision below;
-- (a) Contribution by equal shares. Each insurer pays an equal share until the share of
-- each equals the lowest limit; the rest continue in equal shares until each has paid its
-- limit or the loss is paid. That is: there is one common level, and each insurer pays
-- its limit or that level, whichever is less. With the limits in ascending order, the
-- lowest insurer either holds the level (everyone pays loss / n) or pays its limit in
-- full and drops out.
-- src:254 | (a) Contribution by Equal Shares. If all of such other valid and collectible insurance provides for contribution by
-- src:255 | equal shares, the Company shall not be liable for a greater proportion of such loss than would be payable if each
-- src:256 | insurer contributes an equal share until the share of each insurer equals the lowest applicable limit of liability
-- src:257 | under any one policy or the full amount of the loss is paid, and with respect to any amount of loss not so paid the
-- src:258 | remaining insurers then continue to contribute equal shares of the remaining amount of the loss until each such
-- src:259 | insurer has paid its limit in full or the full amount of the loss is paid.
@ref src:254-259
GIVEN loss   IS A NUMBER
      limits IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the level of equal shares of` loss `among the ascending limits` limits MEANS
    CONSIDER limits
    WHEN EMPTY THEN loss
    WHEN lowest FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF   loss DIVIDED BY count limits AT MOST lowest
        THEN loss DIVIDED BY count limits
        ELSE `the level of equal shares of` (loss MINUS lowest) `among the ascending limits` rest

@ref src:254-259
GIVEN loss           IS A NUMBER
      `our limit`    IS A NUMBER
      `other limits` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Condition 5(a) — the Company's share of` loss `by equal shares, our limit` `our limit` `, other limits` `other limits` MEANS
    IF   loss AT LEAST sum `all limits`
    THEN `our limit`
    ELSE min `our limit` (`the level of equal shares of` loss `among the ascending limits` (sort `all limits`))
    WHERE
        `all limits` MEANS `our limit` FOLLOWED BY `other limits`

-- (b) Contribution by limits: the proportion this Policy's limit bears to the total of
-- all the applicable limits, this Policy's included.
-- src:261 | (b) Contribution by Limits. If any of such other insurance does not provide for contribution by equal shares, the
-- src:262 | Company shall not be liable for a greater proportion of such loss than the applicable limit of liability under this
-- src:263 | Policy for such loss bears to the total applicable limit of liability of all valid and collectible insurance against such
-- src:264 | loss.
@ref src:261-264
GIVEN loss           IS A NUMBER
      `our limit`    IS A NUMBER
      `other limits` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Condition 5(b) — the Company's share of` loss `by limits, our limit` `our limit` `, other limits` `other limits` MEANS
    loss TIMES `our limit` DIVIDED BY (`our limit` PLUS sum `other limits`)

-- The whole of Condition 5. "Primary ... except when stated to apply in excess of or
-- contingent upon the absence of other insurance": where it is so stated is not said, so
-- the basis this Policy applies on is an input.
-- Arm order follows the text: no other insurance on this basis, then (a), then (b).
-- Not covered by the text: this Policy on an excess or contingent basis while other
-- insurance applies on a different basis. That is declined by name (NOTES.md, fork F15).
@ref src:245-264
GIVEN loss                                     IS A NUMBER
      `our limit`                              IS A NUMBER
      `this insurance applies on the basis of` IS A `A basis of insurance`
      others                                   IS A LIST OF `Another insurance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Condition 5 — the most of the loss the Company is liable for, of` loss `with our limit` `our limit` `, on the basis` `this insurance applies on the basis of` `, alongside` others MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   null `others on the same basis` AND (`this insurance applies on the basis of` EQUALS `primary` OR null others)
        THEN loss
        IF   null `others on the same basis`
        THEN `Condition 5 does not say how an excess or contingent insurance shares with insurance on another basis`
        IF   all (GIVEN o YIELD o's `provides for contribution by equal shares`) `others on the same basis`
        THEN `Condition 5(a) — the Company's share of` loss `by equal shares, our limit` `our limit` `, other limits` (map (GIVEN o YIELD o's `the applicable limit of liability`) `others on the same basis`)
        OTHERWISE `Condition 5(b) — the Company's share of` loss `by limits, our limit` `our limit` `, other limits` (map (GIVEN o YIELD o's `the applicable limit of liability`) `others on the same basis`)
    WHERE
        `others on the same basis` MEANS filter (GIVEN o YIELD o's `applies to the loss on the basis of` EQUALS `this insurance applies on the basis of`) others

@ref src:245-252
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Condition 5 does not say how an excess or contingent insurance shares with insurance on another basis` MEANS
    REFUSE "Condition 5 does not say how an excess or contingent insurance shares with insurance on another basis"

§§ `6. Subrogation`

-- src:266 | 6. Subrogation
-- src:268 | In the event of any payment under this Policy, the Company shall be subrogated to all the insured's rights of recovery
-- src:269 | therefor against any person or organization and the insured shall execute and deliver instruments and papers and do
-- src:270 | whatever else is necessary to secure such rights. The insured shall do nothing after loss to prejudice such rights.
@ref src:268-270
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to the policy` `An act under the policy`
`Condition 6 — the insured secures the rights of recovery` MEANS
        PARTY `the insured`
        MUST  `execute and deliver instruments and papers to secure the rights of recovery`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    RAND
        PARTY `the insured`
        SHANT `do something after loss to prejudice the rights of recovery`
        LEST  BREACH BY `the insured` BECAUSE "Condition 6: the insured did something after loss to prejudice the Company's rights of recovery"

§§ `7. Changes`

-- Only an endorsement, signed by an authorized representative of the Company, waives or
-- changes a term; notice to an agent, or an agent's knowledge, does not.
-- src:272 | 7. Changes
-- src:274 | Notice to any agent or knowledge possessed by any agent or by any other person shall not effect a waiver or a change in
-- src:275 | any part of this Policy or stop the Company from asserting any right under the terms of this Policy; nor shall the terms of
-- src:276 | this Policy be waived or changed, except by endorsement issued to form a part of this Policy, signed by an authorized
-- src:277 | representative of the Company.
@ref src:274-277
GIVEN `made by endorsement issued to form a part of this Policy`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `signed by an authorized representative of the Company`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Condition 7 — a waiver or change takes effect` `made by endorsement issued to form a part of this Policy` `,` `signed by an authorized representative of the Company` MEANS
        `made by endorsement issued to form a part of this Policy`
    AND `signed by an authorized representative of the Company`

§§ `8. Assignment`

-- src:279 | 8. Assignment
-- src:281 | Assignment of interest under this Policy shall not bind the Company until its consent is endorsed hereon; if, however,
-- src:282 | the named insured shall die, such insurance as is afforded by this Policy shall apply (1) to the named insured's legal
-- src:283 | representative, as the named insured, but only while acting within the scope of his duties as such, and (2) with respect to
-- src:284 | the property of the named insured, to the person having proper temporary custody thereof, as insured, but only until the
-- src:285 | appointment and qualification of the legal representative.
@ref src:281
GIVEN `the Company's consent is endorsed on the Policy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Condition 8 — an assignment of interest binds the Company` `the Company's consent is endorsed on the Policy` MEANS
    `the Company's consent is endorsed on the Policy`

-- On the named insured's death: (1) the legal representative, as named insured, while
-- acting within the scope of their duties; (2) for the named insured's property, the
-- person having proper temporary custody, until a legal representative is appointed and
-- qualified. Read by Persons Insured in each coverage part.
@ref src:281-285
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Condition 8 — on the named insured's death, the person claimed against is an insured` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `the person claimed against`
    WHEN `the legal representative of the named insured, who has died` THEN
        "(1)" ... `for` claim `,` `the legal representative is acting within the scope of their duties as such`
    WHEN `the person having proper temporary custody of the property of the named insured, who has died` THEN
            "(2)" ... `for` claim `,` `the claim is with respect to the property of the named insured`
        AND NOT `for` claim `,` `a legal representative of the named insured has been appointed and qualified`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `9. Cancellation`

-- The named insured cancels by surrender, or by mailed written notice of a later date.
-- The Company cancels by mailed written notice of a date "not less than ten (10) days
-- thereafter". Mailing is proof of notice; delivery is equal to mailing. The days are
-- calendar days (NOTES.md, fork F16); the tenth day after mailing is allowed.
-- src:287 | 9. Cancellation
-- src:289 | This Policy may be cancelled by the named insured by surrender thereof to the Company or any of its authorized agents
-- src:290 | or by mailing to the Company written notice stating when thereafter the cancellation shall be effective. This Policy may
-- src:291 | be cancelled by the Company by mailing to the named insured at the address shown in this Policy, written notice stating
-- src:292 | when not less than ten (10) days thereafter such cancellation shall be effective. The mailing of notice as aforesaid shall
-- src:293 | be sufficient proof of notice. The time surrender or the effective date and hour of cancellation stated in the notice shall
-- src:294 | become the end of the policy period. Delivery of such written notice either by the named insured or by the Company
-- src:295 | shall be equivalent to mailing.
@ref src:290-292
GIVEN `the date of mailing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Condition 9 — the earliest date the Company's cancellation can take effect, mailed on` `the date of mailing` MEANS
    `the date of mailing` PLUS 10

@ref src:290-293
GIVEN `the date of mailing`        IS A DATE
      `the effective date stated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Condition 9 — the Company's notice, mailed on` `the date of mailing` `, validly states the effective date` `the effective date stated` MEANS
    `the effective date stated` AT LEAST `Condition 9 — the earliest date the Company's cancellation can take effect, mailed on` `the date of mailing`

-- "The time surrender or the effective date and hour of cancellation stated in the notice
-- shall become the end of the policy period": the caller records that date as
-- `the policy period ends` of the policy (nouns).

-- Earned premium on cancellation. The named insured's cancellation uses "the customary
-- short rate table and procedure", which the document does not contain: declined by
-- name. The Company's cancellation is pro rata: the premium times the days elapsed over the
-- days in the period, each counted as the difference of the two dates (NOTES.md, fork F17).
-- src:297 | If the named insured cancels, earned premium shall be computed in accordance with the customary short rate table and
-- src:298 | procedure. If the Company cancels, earned premium shall be computed pro rata. Premium adjustment may be made
-- src:301 | Page 4 of 14
-- src:303 | Revised General Liability Policy Form
-- src:304 | either at the time cancellation is effected or as soon as practicable after cancellation becomes effective, but payment or
-- src:305 | tender of unearned premium is not a condition of cancellation.
@ref src:297
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Condition 9 — the customary short rate table is not in the document` MEANS
    REFUSE "Condition 9: the customary short rate table and procedure are not in the document"

@ref src:297-298
GIVEN premium                   IS A NUMBER
      `the period begins`       IS A DATE
      `the period was to end`   IS A DATE
      `cancellation effective`  IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Condition 9 — the earned premium when the Company cancels, on a premium of` premium `for a period from` `the period begins` `to` `the period was to end` `, cancelled on` `cancellation effective` MEANS
    premium TIMES (Day `cancellation effective` MINUS Day `the period begins`)
            DIVIDED BY (Day `the period was to end` MINUS Day `the period begins`)

@ref src:297-298
GIVEN who                       IS A `A party to the policy`
      premium                   IS A NUMBER
      `the period begins`       IS A DATE
      `the period was to end`   IS A DATE
      `cancellation effective`  IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Condition 9 — the earned premium when` who `cancels, on a premium of` premium `for a period from` `the period begins` `to` `the period was to end` `, cancelled on` `cancellation effective` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `the Company` THEN
        `Condition 9 — the earned premium when the Company cancels, on a premium of` premium `for a period from` `the period begins` `to` `the period was to end` `, cancelled on` `cancellation effective`
    WHEN `the named insured` THEN `Condition 9 — the customary short rate table is not in the document`
    OTHERWISE `Condition 9 gives the right to cancel only to the named insured and the Company`

@ref src:289-292
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Condition 9 gives the right to cancel only to the named insured and the Company` MEANS
    REFUSE "Condition 9 gives the right to cancel only to the named insured and the Company"

-- "Premium adjustment may be made either at the time cancellation is effected or as soon
-- as practicable after": no period, so no WITHIN. Payment is not a condition of
-- cancellation, so the cancellation stands whether or not this duty is performed.
@ref src:298-305
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party to the policy` `An act under the policy`
`Condition 9 — the Company returns the unearned premium` MEANS
    PARTY `the Company`
    MUST  `return the unearned portion of the premium`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§§ `10. Declaration`

-- The named insured's statements in the declarations are agreements and representations,
-- and the Policy is the whole agreement. What follows from an untrue statement the policy
-- does not say; the Law on Insurance Business does (NOTES.md, fork F31).
-- src:307 | 10. Declaration
-- src:309 | By acceptance of this Policy, the named insured agrees that the statements in the declarations are his agreements and
-- src:310 | representations, that this Policy is issued in reliance upon the truth of such representations and that this Policy
-- src:311 | embodies all agreements existing between himself and the Company or any of its agents relating to this insurance.
@ref src:309-311
`Condition 10 — the declaration` MEANS
    "By acceptance of this Policy, the named insured agrees that the statements in the declarations are his agreements and representations, that this Policy is issued in reliance upon the truth of such representations and that this Policy embodies all agreements existing between himself and the Company or any of its agents relating to this insurance."
